# CLAUDE.log — Append-only error log
# Format: [DATE] [FILE] [TYPE] — description + fix applied


[2026-11-20] [data_pipeline/prices/panel.py] [MEMORY] — building the price panel kept every price series in memory; on this 5 GB machine the kernel OOM-killer killed VS Code.
  Fix: per-company series cache, rows trimmed to the needed window early. Run heavy pipeline scripts under a memory cap:
  systemd-run --user --scope -q -p MemoryMax=1500M -p MemorySwapMax=0 .venv/bin/python -I <script>
[2026-11-20] [data_pipeline/prices/validate.py] [BUG] — ticker picked by total validation count: coincidental 3% price matches (AA vs Howmet 2021/2023) won over the continuous ticker, and Yahoo splices two companies under one ticker (AA = Alcoa Inc. until 2016, then Alcoa Corp.).
  Fix: pick by run of consecutive validations, drop isolated contradicted matches, periods never span a non-picked snapshot.
[2026-11-20] [data_pipeline/prices/download.py] [DATA] — Yahoo keeps only a 1-2 row stub for recently delisted tickers (EA, AVB...), cached as if valid.
  Fix: answers of <= 5 rows are not cached; those tickers fall back to Tiingo.
[2026-11-26] [data_pipeline/membership/tickers.py] [BUG] — the Tiingo name of a historical ticker was only tried when Wikipedia had no name; Wikipedia's wording ("Interpublic Group of Companies") sometimes fails to match EDGAR, so IPG, DFS, ETFC, FDO... never got a CIK and their companies had no price.
  Fix: both names are tried (Wikipedia first). Companies still without ticker get fallbacks: tickers declared in their own XBRL reports (sec.trading_symbols) and name-matching hanshof tickers listed while they were held.
[2026-11-26] [data_pipeline/sources/tiingo.py] [DATA] — Tiingo prices by ticker only serve the CURRENT holder of a reused ticker (STI 2018-2019 returns nothing) and sometimes a 1-row stub (WRK). Old holders of reused tickers are not recoverable from Tiingo free.
